{
  "source": {
    "title": "Piano Adventures Correlation Chart (Faber Piano Adventures)",
    "edition": "May 2017 (date printed in the page header; file uploaded 2017/09)",
    "url": "https://pianoadventures.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2017/09/Piano-Adventures-Correlation-Chart.pdf",
    "retrieved": "2026-10-03",
    "meaning": "A publisher's guide (Faber Piano Adventures) to roughly correlating its own method-book levels (Primer, 1, 2A, 2B, 3A, 3B, 4, 5) with other method series and with RCM and ABRSM exam levels; it is not an examination syllabus and states no requirements of its own beyond the topics listed per book level.",
    "pageNumbering": "All 'page' values are PDF page numbers (3-page landscape PDF; page 1 = Primer to Level 2B, page 2 = Level 3A to Level 5, page 3 = end of Level 5 topics and 'Beyond PA 5')."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Column order as printed: Alfred Premier, Alfred Basic, Piano Safari, Bastien 1 - 4, Piano Pronto, Music Tree, HLSP, Celebration Series, RCM Exam, ABRSM Exam. 'HLSP' is printed as an abbreviation and not expanded in the chart.",
    "Cell text is copied as printed, including line breaks rendered as a space after '/' (e.g. 'Prep A/ Prep B'); 'parts' splits on '/' only. Source typos kept verbatim: 'doted quarter note' (Level 2B), 'Level2' (Level 3B, Celebration Series), duplicate topic 'V7 chord in root position' listed twice (Level 4).",
    "Blank cells in the source are recorded as value:null with blankInSource:true; no value was inferred for them (blank: Primer RCM/ABRSM/Celebration; Level 1 ABRSM; Level 2A HLSP and ABRSM; Level 2B ABRSM; Level 4 Piano Safari, HLSP; Level 5 Piano Safari, Bastien, HLSP; Beyond PA 5 all but Piano Pronto, Celebration, RCM, ABRSM).",
    "The chart's RCM column calls levels 'Prep A', 'Prep B' for Primer-2B and then 'Grade 1', 'Grade 2', 'Grade 3' for Levels 3A onward, while the Celebration Series column uses 'Level N'. RCM's own syllabus names its levels 'Level N' (not 'Grade N'); the chart's 'Grade' wording is kept as printed and not reconciled. Faber Level 3A and 3B both map to RCM 'Grade 1'; Faber 3B maps to Celebration 'Level 1/ Level2' and to ABRSM 'Grade 1/ Grade 2'.",
    "All cells were read from a 140 dpi render of each page; the column alignment was unambiguous in the image (ruled table), so no cell is marked uncertain. The pdftotext output was not used for cell assignment because tab-separated columns were ambiguous in it.",
    "Topic superscripts (e.g. 8th, 2nd) are flattened to plain text; the en dash in '16th–note rhythm patterns' is as printed. The chart gives no key signatures beyond those named in topics and no tempo or exam-task information."
  ],
